-- ============================================================================
-- DR2 PROFESSIONAL DEEP SEED: Torque, Drag & Casing Wear, intermediate tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed, so the seeded structure and the
-- shipped lesson files cannot disagree.
--
-- What this tier owns: the one number in the model that nobody measured. A
-- friction FACTOR is not a coefficient of friction: it absorbs genuine sliding
-- friction, the bending stiffness soft string discarded, cuttings beds, and
-- every other omission, so its TREND is informative while its VALUE is not a
-- material property. Which factor matters depends on where the side force is,
-- so a cased-hole factor on a well whose shoe sits in the vertical section
-- multiplies zero. Rotating does not reduce friction, it redirects it, through
-- one pair of direction cosines set by the ratio of trip speed to tool joint
-- surface speed; the moment arm is the TOOL JOINT radius and using the pipe
-- body understates the torque by 24.53 percent. Side force is largest near the
-- TOP of a build, not at total depth. Calibration is bisection over a monotone
-- response and it ALWAYS succeeds, which is what makes it useful and what
-- makes it dangerous, so the discipline is to fit one observation and predict
-- another. And the comparison against the independent oracle, where refining
-- the step separates discretisation from a model difference and the one
-- closed-form case says which implementation is closer.
--
-- Every number in the lessons is derived by running the vendored
-- engines/drilling against its own goldens, and the teaching lab that the
-- panels and this course share is pinned to the same values by
-- torquedragLab.test.js. A numeric sweep over the lessons resolved all 403
-- literals carrying seven or more significant figures to an engine-derived
-- value; a tier-leakage sweep over the lessons and the banks reports zero
-- downward leaks and zero same-tier answer prints against all eighteen graded
-- fields.
--
-- Answer keys live only here and in academy_quiz_questions, which has no
-- client SELECT policy.
-- ============================================================================

values ('torquedrag', 'intermediate', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-the-friction-factor","title":"The Friction Factor","lesson_keys":["l01-what-it-is-and-is-not","l02-where-the-numbers-come-from","l03-cased-and-open-hole","l04-what-it-hides","l05-the-sweep"]},{"key":"m02-torque","title":"Torque","lesson_keys":["l01-why-rotating-splits-the-friction","l02-the-radius-that-matters","l03-surface-torque-against-depth","l04-off-bottom-and-on-bottom","l05-rotating-while-you-trip"]},{"key":"m03-side-force","title":"Side Force","lesson_keys":["l01-where-it-is-largest","l02-doglegs-and-tension","l03-the-tangent-that-costs-nothing","l04-three-dimensional-turns"]},{"key":"m04-calibration","title":"Calibration","lesson_keys":["l01-backing-it-out-of-a-trip","l02-it-always-succeeds","l03-what-a-fitted-factor-absorbs","l04-predicting-torque-from-a-hookload","l05-two-factors-and-one-observation"]},{"key":"m05-against-the-oracle","title":"Against the Oracle","lesson_keys":["l01-what-the-goldens-are","l02-where-the-two-implementations-part","l03-refining-the-step","l04-the-case-that-settles-it"]},{"key":"m06-the-professional-reading","title":"The Professional Reading","lesson_keys":["l01-the-story-so-far","l02-working-the-capstone","l03-onward"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
